<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Veliocasses</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 57 BCE (approx.) · capital Rotomagus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Belgic people of the lower Seine whose town Rotomagus became Rouen.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Veliocasses held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vexin">Vexin</a> and the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> valley. Caesar reports that they promised warriors to the Belgic league of 57 BCE together with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/viromandui">Viromandui</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their rulers. Their position on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> gave them a share of river trade to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">Channel</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They submitted in 57 BCE and later sent men to relieve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alesia">Alesia</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their chief town <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rotomagus</a> grew into an important river port, the origin of Rouen, later capital of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-normandy">Duchy of Normandy</a>. Their name survives in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vexin">Vexin</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 300 BCE – 57 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:53.73%;width:4.84%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 57 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rotomagus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=veliocasses" aria-label="Veliocasses on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4705 455 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Veliocasses lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5025 711L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5025 711h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5025 711h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Rotomagus. <a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=veliocasses">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

